        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Z5cfQ",
          "name": "For review",
          "width": 900,
          "fill": "$bg",
          "cornerRadius": "$r-xl",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "padding": 24,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "RhcJn",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$text",
              "content": "First read",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "k8KmX",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• A · Alcove is the strongest: one idea (the carrel's walls make a C, the dot is the reader), and it survives 16px in both toolbars.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X16rs5",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D · Bookmark is the friendliest and most ownable letterform, but the notch blurs below 32px.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "yPw2g",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• E · Niche is the most literal 'library', and too detailed for the toolbar; could be an illustration, not the mark.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "C4sydC",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B · Lamp breaks apart at small sizes. C · Shelf is close to Lucide's library icon, which the app already uses for the Library, so it would be confusing.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "q3xyKi",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• Wordmark: Geist lowercase matches the product best. Newsreader is worth keeping in mind for the store listing and website only.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "qYobg",
              "name": "Title 2",
              "fill": "$text",
              "content": "Bookmark round",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "z8pfuG",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D5 · Bookmark and dot is the cleanest: a silhouette everyone recognises, the dot survives 16px, and it links back to the Alcove idea (the point you saved).",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PCrXR",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D2 · Cut-out c says 'Carrel' outright, but the c closes up below 32px; it could be the store/large icon while D5 is the toolbar glyph.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "mkgHc",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D6 · Two ribbons conveys a collection and stays legible small, but sits close to generic 'bookmarks' icons.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "R40fss",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• D1 is the original, slightly cleaner; the notch still blurs at 16px. D3 reads as an 'a', D4 and D7 are too busy, D8 doesn't read as a bookmark.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hsZKK",
              "name": "Title 3",
              "fill": "$text",
              "content": "C-first round",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LFtVL",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• C3 · Ribbon in the counter keeps a bold C and adds a small bookmark in the opening: the clearest mix, and the bookmark is still visible at 32px. At 16px it becomes a C with a dot, which is still fine.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "q3K0Z",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• C1 · Notched terminal is the most refined: a plain, strong C whose lower end is cut like a ribbon tail. Recognisable as a C at every size; the notch is a detail you notice up close.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "jBS4z",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• C6 · Cut-out bookmark is subtle and elegant at large sizes; the cut-out disappears in the toolbar.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "d04hKL",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• C4 reads as ¢ and C5 as ç, so both are out. C2 lost the bookmark entirely, and C8 is messy. C7 is a sturdier, boxier version of C1.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "b7E9zh",
              "name": "Title 4",
              "fill": "$text",
              "content": "D2 round",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Lkx8u",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B1 · Wide fixes D2's problem: the squatter bookmark leaves room for a big c, and it's the only one where the c stays open in the 16px toolbar. It also sits most comfortably beside the wordmark.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iuso9",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B2 · Big c is the most striking at 48px and up, but the thin frame around the c gets fragile at 16px.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X9NC7I",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B3 · Open c is clever (the c can't close), but the channel through the edge makes it read as a key or a plug.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iOUPI",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B4 · Capital C is close to B2 with a rounder letter; no clear gain over the lowercase c.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "JFYs9",
              "name": "Point",
              "fill": "$text-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "• B5–B8 are empty: the pen.dev plan's image generations ran out.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
